{
    "background_story": "Tadeo was a renowned botanist with a passion for aquatic plants. He spent most of his career studying the unique properties of Menyanthaceae, a family of flowering plants that thrive in wet environments. Tadeo's research focused on the bogbean, a particularly fascinating species within the Menyanthaceae family. He traveled to remote wetlands to collect and analyze samples, uncovering new insights into the plant's adaptability and medicinal potential. Tadeo's groundbreaking work led to the development of new treatments for waterborne diseases, earning him international recognition and accolades. His dedication to the study of Menyanthaceae not only advanced the field of botany but also improved the lives of people living in areas where access to clean water is scarce.",
